<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otrar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Farab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otrar was a medieval oasis city on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a> in southern Kazakhstan, an important town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. In 1218 its governor massacred a caravan of merchants sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, the incident that provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-the-khwarazmian-empire">Mongol invasion of the Khwarazmian Empire</a>; the city fell after a long siege. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> died there in February 1405 as he marched to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Its ruins are now an archaeological site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otrar.jpg" alt="Otrar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Coopypasted · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%93%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B8%D1%89%D0%B5_%D0%9E%D1%82%D1%8B%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%80_%D1%81_%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B4%D1%83%D1%85%D0%B0.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the governor of <b>Otrar</b> massacred a Mongol-sponsored caravan in 1218, the shah executed the envoy sent to demand redress, provoking a devastating invasion.</blockquote><a href="/empire/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…he governed chiefly through terror, the speed of his armies and the appointment of sons and grandsons to regional commands, an arrangement that bred the succession struggles which began tearing the empire apart after his death at <b>Otrar</b> in February 1405, as he marched to invade Ming China.</blockquote><a href="/empire/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
